{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 8. Re1. Re1 supports e4 and makes e5 more credible. Black has a broad d5-c5 center and may expand on the queenside while White builds a kingside initiative. Black can play ...Qc7, ...b5 or ...dxe4. A kingside attack is premature if e4 can simply be captured. } 8. Re1 Qc7 9. c3 h6 10. Qe2 Rd8 *

