[SetUp "1"]

{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 9. e5. Advancing e5 gains space and displaces Nf6, but fixes a pawn that Black can undermine with ...f6. The f1 knight route is now a plan, not a forced continuation. Black can strike at the base or head of the chain. A dramatic wing attack fails if the center opens with your pieces misplaced. } 9. e5 Nd7 10. Qe2 b5 *

