{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 6. Nbd2. Black develops the light-squared bishop before closing it with ...e6. White cannot assume that Black has the restricted bishop of a French-type position. The bishop on f5 influences e4 and may move to g6 if chased. A knight trip can cost more time than the bishop is worth. } 6. Nbd2 h6 7. c4 Be7 8. b4 O-O *

