{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 7. dxc4. White changes the usual KIA pawn structure to challenge Black's center immediately. The d-pawn recapture opens the d-file and retains a central foothold. Black can exchange queens or use ...Nbd7 and ...Be7 to complete development. The position is now closer to a Reti structure than an e5 attack. } 7. dxc4 Qxd1 8. Rxd1 Bc2 9. Rd2 Bf5 *

